          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: la grève",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "la grève — \"the strike\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Les trains ne roulent pas: il y a une grève. The trains are not running: there is a strike."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Faire grève, être en grève — to be on strike. La grève is also a sandy shore."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "grève \"strike\" is built on grève \"sandy shore\": the usual explanation is a riverside square of that name where people looking for work gathered. The origin of grève \"shore\" is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
